    "why_not_native": "native silently degrades to a generic microarchitecture on a compiler that does not know the host CPU",
    "minimum_toolchain": "GCC 14.1 or Clang 19",
    "measurement_node": "single-socket AMD EPYC 4545P, 16 cores, SMT off, one NUMA node",
    "binary_sha256_in_experiment_fingerprint": true,
    "level_compaction_dynamic_level_bytes": false,
    "io": {
      "use_direct_reads": false,
      "use_direct_io_for_flush_and_compaction": false,
      "compaction_readahead_size_bytes": 2097152,
      "swept": false,
      "amended": "2026-09-12, in place, before any Gate 1 run",
      "reason": "pinned off on measured cost. On the measurement node at 10M T=2, mixgraph ran at 2750 ops/s with direct I/O and 58332 ops/s buffered, a 21x penalty putting the Gate 1 sweep near 95 hours.",
      "consequence": "the host page cache holds the database, so latency, runtime and stall figures are warm-cache and are reported as such. They bound foreground disruption; they are not storage latency claims.",
      "unaffected_metrics": [
        "write_amplification",
        "point_read_amplification",
        "space_amplification",
        "sorted_run_seeks_per_scan",
        "per_level_merge_survival",
        "capacity_space_curve"
      ],
      "revisit": "may be set true for the final paper benchmark workload if the amplification results justify the cost. Such runs carry fingerprint field dio1, cannot be pooled with dio0 runs, and need their own comparator manifest because stage 06 selects on runtime, which is cache-sensitive.",
      "rejected_alternative": "a cgroup memory cap on the benchmark process. It is external state the fingerprint cannot carry and a new lease silently loses.",
      "recorded_in": [
        "experiment_fingerprint: dio field",
        "metadata.env: use_direct_io"
      ],
      "measured": {
        "node": "AMD EPYC 4545P, buffered vs direct, 10M T=2 mixgraph",
        "buffered_ops_per_second": 58332,
        "direct_ops_per_second_max_open_files_unlimited": 2750,
        "direct_ops_per_second_max_open_files_1000": 1960,
        "penalty": "21x"
      },
      "correction": "an earlier revision of this entry quoted a 2.6x penalty. That compared the direct-I/O pilot on this node against a buffered figure from the 2026-09-03 suite, which ran on different hardware. The cross-machine comparison was invalid; the same-node penalty is 21x. Recorded rather than silently replaced."
    }
